      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 1
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "Welcome! In this experiment, you\u2019ll learn how to control the position
        of a DC motor using a PID controller.\n<br></br>\nYou will investigate the
        effects of Proportional (Kp), Integral (Ki), and Derivative (Kd) gains on
        the system's response."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: This experiment aims to understand the principles of PID control by
        adjusting its three parameters (Kp, Ki, Kd).<br><br>You will investigate
        how each gain affects system performance.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency switch on the experimental model.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Switch on the experimental model using the ON/OFF switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: 'Set_Gains_01 '
      value: Set the Proportional Gain (Kp) to 1, Integral Gain (Ki) to 0, and Derivative
        Gain (Kd) to 0.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetPoint_120
      value: Set the desired position (setpoint) to 120 mm in the designated field.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: Click the 'Start' button to initiate the motor movement.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Reset_Button_01
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_02
      value: "Set the gains to: Kp = 25\u060C Ki = 20\u060C Kd = 0.2."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: click 'Start' again.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pause_Button
      value: Pause the run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button
      value: Save Screen.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Reset_button_02
      value: Click on reset button.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: What is the primary effect of increasing the Proportional gain (Kp)?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: Eliminates steady-state error
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: Reduces rise time but may increase overshoot
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: Slows down system response
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: Which PID term is primarily responsible for eliminating steady-state
        error?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: Proportional (Kp)
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: Derivative (Kd)
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: Integral (Ki)
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: Observe the system's response on the graph. Note the rise time, overshoot,
        and steady-state error.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: Observe the system's response on the graph. Note the rise time, overshoot,
        and steady-state error.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: 'You have finished Experiment 1: PID! You can now analyze your results
        or select another experiment.'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_D
      value: All of the above
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_03
      value: This mode depends on determining the motor position along the ruler
        by applying a constant voltage and calculating the time required for the
        motor to reach a desired point. The voltage is then disconnected after this
        time, and the final position reached by the motor is observed.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: 'Notification_04

'
      value: Use this mode when you want to drive the motor by direct voltage input,
        not by a position setting on the ruler.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6be66fa07a46b1c4c8128c7abcecfd3f, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: DC Motor Positioning using Manual mode
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 2
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "Welcome! In this mode, you\u2019ll manually control the DC motor\u2019s
        position using software inputs in an open-loop configuration meaning there
        is no feedback or automatic correction. You\u2019ll directly send commands
        to the motor and observe how it responds, helping you understand the limitations
        and behavior of open-loop control."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: "To manually command the DC motor\u2019s position using open-loop control,
        observe the resulting angular motion in real time, and analyze how the absence
        of feedback affects positioning accuracy, repeatability, and system response."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency switch on the experimental model.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Switch on the experimental model using the ON/OFF switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Manual_Mode_Button
      value: Active the manual mode by clicking on manual mode button
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Move_Slider_10
      value: Move the slider to set a desired output (120).
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_To_Voltage
      value: Activate switch in direction of Voltage
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Voltage_9
      value: Set the voltage to 9 V
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button
      value: Click on Start button
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Stop_Button
      value: Click on Stop button
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished! You can now select another experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: What is the main characteristic of an open-loop control system like
        the one used in this manual mode?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: It uses sensor feedback to correct errors automatically.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: It operates based on a preset sequence without using the actual output
        for correction.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: It requires continuous human input for each operation.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: In manual (open-loop) mode, what happens if the motor encounters an
        unexpected load or friction?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: The system automatically increases power to maintain the set position.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: 'The motor''s position may deviate and will NOT be corrected automatically. '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: The software will trigger an alarm and shut down the system.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: Observe the position of the slide on the scale. Note that the system
        does not automatically correct its position.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pause_Button
      value: Pause the run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pause_Voltage
      value: Pause the input voltage by pressing pause next to the voltage input
        field.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: This mode depends on determining the motor position along the ruler
        by applying a constant voltage and calculating the time required for the
        motor to reach a desired point. The voltage is then disconnected after this
        time, and the final position reached by the motor is observed.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_03
      value: Use this mode when you want to drive the motor by direct voltage input,
        not by a position setting on the ruler.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a6d180dd5ebbdbb4db506ef461775b09, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Moving_Slider_Def
      value: A carriage that travels along the guide to indicate or set position.
        It is driven by the motor and contacts limit or position sensors.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: ON_OFF_Button_Def
      value: "A control pushbutton that enables or disables the trainer\u2019s motor
        control circuit."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Motor_Indication_LED_Def
      value: An LED that shows motor status by color or blink pattern.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Scale_Def
      value: A fixed graduated ruler that provides a visual reference for slider
        position.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Emergency_Button_Def
      value: A latching, mushroom-head pushbutton that cuts power to motion instantly
        for safety.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Ultrasonic_Sensor_Def
      value: 'A non-contact distance sensor that uses high-frequency sound waves
        to measure the distance to an object by calculating the echo return time.Power
        Screw '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Power_Screw_Def
      value: A lead/ball screw that converts motor rotation into precise linear motion
        of the slider.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: 'Moving_Slider_Title '
      value: Moving Slider
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Scale_Title
      value: Scale
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: 'Emergency_Button_Title '
      value: Emergency Button
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: ON_OFF_Button_Title
      value: ON/OFF Button
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Motor_Indication_LED_Title
      value: Motor Indication LED
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: 'DC_Motor_Title '
      value: DC Motor
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Ultrasonic_Sensor_Title
      value: Ultrasonic Sensor
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Power_Screw_Title
      value: Power Screw
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: DC_Motor_Def
      value: Converts DC power to rotation using magnetic fields and commutation.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Limit_Switches_Title
      value: Limit Switches
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Limit_Switches_Def
      value: Electromechanical switches that change contacts when the slider reaches
        an end position to stop or reverse motion.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Soft_Membrane_Linear_Potentiometer_Title
      value: Soft Membrane Linear Potentiometer
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Soft_Membrane_Linear_Potentiometer_Def
      value: Thin flexible strip that outputs position as a variable resistance or
        voltage divider.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4449ca77052704a4d9586dff55a9ec44, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: 'Level Control in Open-Loop

        (Manual Mode)'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 2
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "Welcome! In this experiment, you\u2019ll manually control the water
        level in a tank using open-loop control meaning no feedback or automatic
        correction is used. \n\nYou will directly set the pump speed and valve position
        to influence the liquid level and observe how the system responds without
        PID intervention."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: To manually control the water level by adjusting pump and valve settings
        in open-loop mode, observe system behavior, and understand the limitations
        of open-loop control such as sensitivity to disturbances and inability to
        correct steady-state errors.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency button.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Press the trainer ON/OFF switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Manual_Mode_Button
      value: "Click the \u201COpen-Loop Mode\u201D button to disable PID and enter
        open-loop control."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Move_Pump_Slider_20
      value: Set the pump speed to 60% using the manual pump slider.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Move_Level_Slider_80
      value: Set the desired level of the water to 40 mm using the Level slider.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Use_Level_Slider_Mode
      value: Activate switch in direction of Level
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Save_Screen
      value: "Click \u201CSave Screen\u201D to capture the current tank level and
        manual settings."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: Click Start to begin the process.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: Since this is open-loop control, the system will NOT automatically adjust
        pump or valve if the level drifts. You must manually correct it.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pause_Pump
      value: Click on pause button to stop the pump operation
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: Since this is open-loop control, the system will NOT automatically adjust
        pump or valve if the level drifts. You must manually correct it.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Stop_Button
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: Click Start again
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished! You can now analyze your results or select another
        experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: What is the main characteristic of an open-loop control system?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: It uses sensor feedback to correct errors automatically.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: It requires constant human input to operate.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: 'Its output does not affect the control action (no feedback). '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: In open-loop level control, what happens if a disturbance (e.g., valve
        leakage) occurs?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: The PID controller compensates automatically.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: The level changes and is NOT corrected automatically.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: The pump shuts off immediately.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_03
      value: This mode depends on determining the level along the scale by applying
        a constant pump power and calculating the time required for the device to
        reach a desired level. The pump power is then disconnected after this time,
        and the final level reached by the device is observed.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_04
      value: Use this mode when you want to drive the device by direct pump power,
        not by a flow rate value on the slider.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Disturbance_01
      value: "Set disturbance to 40% using the \u201CDisturbance%\u201D slider."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Export_button
      value: "Click \u201CExport\u201D to save the data to excel sheet."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Disturbance_02
      value: "Set disturbance to 70% using the \u201CDisturbance%\u201D slider."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 74e04707cfcfcfb43a49b0b47c2a3ec0, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: 'Level Control using PID

        (Automatic Mode)'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Expirement 1
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "In this experiment, you\u2019ll learn how to control the liquid level
        in the upper tank using a PID controller. You will investigate how the Proportional
        (Kp), Integral (Ki), and Derivative (Kd) gains affect the system\u2019s ability
        to reach and maintain a desired level. This demonstrates closed-loop feedback
        control in a real industrial process."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: To understand PID control principles by adjusting Kp, Ki, and Kd gains
        to regulate the liquid level in the tank. You will analyze how each parameter
        influences rise time, overshoot, settling time, and steady-state error.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency button
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Press the trainer ON/OFF switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_01
      value: 'Set the PID gains: (Kp) to 2000, (Ki) to 500, and (Kd) to 0.'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetPoint_10
      value: Set the desired level (setpoint) to 80 mm.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: Click Start to begin the control process.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetValve_60
      value: Manually increase the valve opening to 50% to simulate a disturbance.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Reset_Button_01
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_02
      value: Adjust Kd to 4000 to improve system response.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: Click Start again.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button
      value: "Click \u201CSave Screen\u201D to capture the current response curve."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished! You can now analyze your results or select another
        experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: Which PID term is primarily responsible for eliminating steady-state
        error?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: Proportional (Kp)
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: Derivative (Kd)
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: Integral (Ki)
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: 'Increasing Kd generally:'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: 'Observe the system response: note rise time, overshoot, and steady-state
        error.'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: Increases steady-state error
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: Reduces overshoot and improves stability
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: Eliminates all noise
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: 'Compare responses: Did Ki eliminate steady-state error? Did Kd reduce
        overshoot?'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Export_Button
      value: "Click \u201CExport\u201D to save the data to excel sheet."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pause_Button
      value: "Click \u201CPause\u201D to pause the current run"
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Alarm_Critical_Level_Reached
      value: 'Warning: Tank level is 90% full. Simulation paused for safety until
        the level is safe.'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_03
      value: 'This mode depends on determining the level along the scale by applying
        a constant pump power and calculating the time required for the device to
        reach a desired level.

        The pump power is then disconnected after
        this time, and the final level reached by the device is observed.'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_04
      value: Use this mode when you want to drive the device by direct pump power,
        not by a flow rate value on the scale.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f0d520b6e2a9d544cbc62631bbb3b895, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Main_Tank_Def
      value: Reservoir that stores process liquid and sets static head to achieve
        the desired level using immersed pump.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Level_Tank_Def
      value: A tank that contains scale to ensure the reading of the water level.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Immersed_Pump_Def
      value: DC pump that drives water to the level tank.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
