  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0c530181cd118714f82b4f24ccfb0704, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: DC_Motor_Title
      value: DC Motor
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: DC_Motor_Def
      value: A DC motor converts direct electrical power into rotary motion using
        magnetic fields and commutation.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Inductive_Proximity_Sensor_Title
      value: Inductive Proximity Sensor
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Inductive_Proximity_Sensor_Def
      value: A non-contact sensor that detects metal targets by inducing eddy currents
        and measuring field change.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Generator_Title
      value: Generator
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Generator_Def
      value: A machine that converts mechanical input from the shaft into electrical
        output. In this trainer it acts as a load and speed sensor source.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Speed_Digital_Display_Title
      value: 'Speed Digital Display '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Speed_Digital_Display_Def
      value: Panel meter that shows motor speed from a sensor or tachogenerator input.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Emergency_Switch_Title
      value: Emergency Switch
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Emergency_Switch_Def
      value: Latching mushroom pushbutton that removes power to motion for safety.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: ON_OFF_Button_Title
      value: On/Off Switch
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: ON_OFF_Button_Def
      value: Front-panel pushbutton that enables or disables the control circuit.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Motor_Indication_LED_Title
      value: Motor Indication LED
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Motor_Indication_LED_Def
      value: LED that indicates motor status by color or blink pattern.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Generator_Indication_LED_Title
      value: Generator Indication LED
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Generator_Indication_LED_Def
      value: LED that indicates generator presence or mode, such as active load or
        signal OK.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 324c2c63599c8d2418e0082e139b32e5, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: DC Motor Speed PID Control
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 1
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "Welcome! In this experiment, you\u2019ll learn how to control the speed
        of a DC motor using a PID controller. You will investigate the effects of
        Proportional (Kp), Integral (Ki), and Derivative (Kd) gains, and apply a
        load disturbance to observe the controller\u2019s ability to reject it and
        maintain setpoint."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: This experiment aims to understand PID control by adjusting Kp, Ki,
        and Kd to optimize speed response, eliminate steady-state error, reject disturbances.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Switch on the ON/OFF switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_01
      value: Set Kp = 0.001, Ki = 500, Kd = 0.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetPoint_01
      value: Set the desired position (setpoint) to 1500 RPM.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: Click the 'Start' button to initiate the motor movement.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Disturbance
      value: "Set disturbance to 30% using the \u201CDisturbance%\u201D slider."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Reset_Button_01
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_02
      value: Adjust Ki = 10
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: Click Start again.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button
      value: "Click \u201CSave Screen\u201D to capture the current response curve."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished the DC Motor Speed PID Control experiment! You can
        now analyze your results or select another experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Export_Button
      value: "Click \u201CExport\u201D to save the data to excel sheet."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: Observe the system's response on the graph. Note the rise time, overshoot,
        and steady-state error.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: Observe the generator effect on the DC motor Speed and the system response.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: 'Pop-up Quiz: What is the primary purpose of the Proportional (P) term
        in a PID controller?'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: To eliminate steady-state error over time
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: To predict future errors and dampen the system
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: 'To produce an output proportional to the current error '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: Which of the following best describes the role of the Derivative (Kd)
        term in a PID controller?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: It eliminates the accumulated past error.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: 'It produces a correction based on the rate of change of the error. '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: It provides a constant offset to the controller output.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fcaec22566f1e804f8ea7c0dbb75bdaa, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: DC Motor Speed using Manual mode
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 2
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "Welcome! In this mode, you\u2019ll manually control the DC motor\u2019s
        speed using software inputs in an open-loop configuration meaning there is
        no feedback or automatic correction. You\u2019ll directly send commands to
        the motor and observe how it responds, helping you understand the limitations
        and behavior of open-loop control."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: "To manually command the DC motor\u2019s speed using open-loop control,
        observe the resulting speed in real time, and analyze how the absence of
        feedback affects positioning accuracy, repeatability, and system response."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Switch on the ON/OFF switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Manual_Mode_Button
      value: "Click the \u201COpen-Loop Mode\u201D button to disable PID and enter
        open-loop control."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetSpeed_01
      value: Set the desired speed to 1200 RPM
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: Click the 'Start' button to initiate the motor movement.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Stop_Button_01
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Use_VoltageOnly_Mode
      value: Activate switch in direction of Voltage.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: Click Start again
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Disturbance_01
      value: "Set disturbance to 90% using the \u201CDisturbance%\u201D slider."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button
      value: "Click \u201CSave Screen\u201D to capture the current response curve."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Export_button
      value: " Click \u201CExport\u201D to save the data to excel sheet."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished! You can now analyze your results or select another
        experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: Note that the system does not automatically correct its position.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: Observe the generator effect on the DC motor Speed and the system response.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: In manual (open-loop) mode, what happens if the motor encounters an
        unexpected load or friction?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: The system automatically increases power to maintain the set position.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: 'The motor''s position may deviate and will NOT be corrected automatically. '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: The software will trigger an alarm and shut down the system.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Use_VoltageAndRuler_Mode
      value: Activate switch in direction of ruler
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_InputField
      value: Set the voltage to 9 V.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: What is the main characteristic of an open-loop control system?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: It uses sensor feedback to correct errors automatically.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: It requires constant human input to operate.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: Its output does not affect the control action (no feedback).
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_03
      value: This mode depends on determining the motor speed along the ruler by
        applying a constant voltage and calculating the time required for the motor
        to reach a desired RPM. The voltage is then disconnected after this time,
        and the final speed reached by the motor is observed.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_04
      value: Use this mode when you want to drive the motor by direct voltage input,
        not by a speed value on the ruler.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 93e2af971aa79d04598466361dc9472b, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Emergency_Switch_Title
      value: Emergency Switch
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Emergency_Switch_Def
      value: The emergency switch is a safety feature that immediately disconnects
        the power to the entire system, stopping all operations in case of an emergency.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: ON_OFF_Button_Title
      value: Trainer On/Off Switch
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: ON_OFF_Button_Def
      value: The trainer on/off switch controls the power to the entire Pressure
        Process Control Trainer system, allowing it to be turned on or off for operation
        and safety.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Diaphragm_Pump_Title
      value: Diaphragm Pump
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Diaphragm_Pump_Def
      value: The diaphragm pump delivers a hermetic seal between the drive mechanism
        and the compression chamber, allowing the pump to transfer, compress, and
        evacuate the medium without the need for lubrication. The diaphragm pump
        can produce discharge pressures as high as 1200 bar.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pressure_Vessel_Title
      value: Pressure Vessel
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pressure_Vessel_Def
      value: The pressure vessel holds the medium (such as air or water) under controlled
        pressure. It is used for storing the medium while maintaining a stable pressure
        for testing or control processes.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pressure_Gauge_Title
      value: Pressure Gauge
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pressure_Gauge__Def
      value: "The pressure gauge measures and displays the pressure inside the pressure
        vessel, allowing for real-time monitoring of the system\u2019s performance."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Proportional_Solenoid_Valve_Title
      value: Proportional Solenoid Valve
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Proportional_Solenoid_Valve_Def
      value: "The proportional solenoid valve regulates the flow of the medium in
        the system by adjusting the valve\u2019s position proportionally to the input
        signal, allowing precise control over flow rates and pressure."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Needle_Valve_Title
      value: ' Needle Valve'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Needle_Valve_Def
      value: "The needle valve provides fine adjustment of the flow and pressure
        by allowing precise control over the fluid path, ideal for fine-tuning the
        system\u2019s pressure levels."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Valve_Indication_LED_Title
      value: Valve Indication LED
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Valve_Indication_LED_Def
      value: The valve indication LED shows the status of the proportional solenoid
        valve by lighting up when the valve is open, providing a visual indicator
        of the valve's operation.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pump_Indication_LED_Title
      value: Pump Indication LED
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pump_Indication_LED_Def
      value: The pump indication LED provides a visual status of the diaphragm pump,
        lighting up when the pump is running and providing operational feedback.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bee86a706d14d5d4ba0b88cd4d9bf00d, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: 'Pressure Control using PID

        (Automatic Mode)'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 1
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "Welcome! In this experiment, you\u2019ll explore how a PID controller
        manages air pressure in a closed system. You\u2019ll adjust proportional,
        integral, and derivative gains to observe their effects on system response
        such as rise time, overshoot, and steady-state error using real-time software
        tools."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: To understand the effects of PID controller parameters (Kp, Ki, Kd)
        on pressure control dynamics and to achieve a stable, accurate system response
        by tuning these gains using the software interface.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Turn on the power switch of the unit.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_01
      value: Set Kp = 120, Ki = 0, Kd = 0.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetPoint_01
      value: Set the desired pressure to 0.5 bar.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: Click the 'Start' button to initiate the Pump.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button
      value: "Click \u201CSave Screen\u201D to capture the current response curve."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Reset_Button_01
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_02
      value: Adjust Ki = 35, Kd = 5.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: Click Start again.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Disturbance
      value: "Set the valve to 30% using the \u201CDisturbance%\u201D slider."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Export_Button
      value: "Click \u201CExport\u201D to save the data to excel sheet."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished! You can now analyze your results or select another
        experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: Observe the system's response on the graph. Note the rise time, overshoot,
        and steady-state error.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: What is the primary purpose of the derivative term (Kd) in a PID controller?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: To reduce overshoot and improve stability.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: To eliminate steady-state error.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: To increase system noise.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: Which PID parameter most directly affects steady-state error?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: Kp
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: Ki
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: Kd
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3c00e5ce877b9364392e9e06cad4d092, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Tank_Title
      value: Tank
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Tank_Def
      value: A reservoir that stores process liquid and allows continuous circulation
        of water within the closed-loop system and helps visualize the flow process.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Rotameter_Title
      value: Rotameter
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Rotameter_Def
      value: A variable-area flowmeter with a float that rises with flow to indicate
        rate on a scale.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pump_Title
      value: Pump
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pump_Def
      value: 'The pump functions as the actuator of the system. It drives the water
        through the piping network by converting electrical energy into hydraulic
        energy. Pump power is adjusted by the controller or manually by the user
        to regulate the flow rate. '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Flowmeter_Sensor_Title
      value: Flowmeter Sensor
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Flowmeter_Sensor_Def
      value: The flowmeter sensor measures the actual flow rate electronically and
        sends this signal to the controller. It serves as the feedback element in
        closed-loop control, enabling accurate comparison between the measured flow
        and the set point.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Proportional_Valve_Title
      value: Proportional Valve
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Proportional_Valve_Def
      value: Electrically actuated valve that modulates opening to regulate flow.
        It used to control flow resistance in the system and acts as a disturbance
        element, allowing controlled restriction of flow to study system response,
        controller performance, and disturbance rejection.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Schematic_Diagram_Title
      value: Schematic Diagram
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Schematic_Diagram_Def
      value: 'The schematic diagram displayed on the front panel represents the process
        flow and control loop. It helps users understand the system layout, signal
        flow, and interaction between the controller, sensor, actuator, and process. '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pump_Indication_LED_Title
      value: Pump Indication LED
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pump_Indication_LED_Def
      value: This LED indicates the operational status of the pump. When illuminated,
        it confirms that the pump is running and supplying flow to the system.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Valve_Indication_LED_Title
      value: Valve Indication LED
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Valve_Indication_LED_Def
      value: 'This LED shows the status of the proportional valve. It provides a
        quick visual indication of valve activation during disturbance experiments. '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Emergency_Button_Title
      value: 'Emergency Button '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Emergency_Button_Def
      value: The emergency button is a safety feature that immediately shuts down
        system operation in case of abnormal conditions or user error. It ensures
        safe operation of the trainer.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: ON_OFF_Trainer_Switch_Title
      value: 'ON/OFF Trainer Switch '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: ON_OFF_Trainer_Switch_Def
      value: "Front-panel switch that enables or disables the trainer\u2019s power
        supply."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 448b21e81e55d3345b80cf749c26107b, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: 'Flow Control using PID

        (Automatic Mode)'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 1
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "Welcome! In this experiment, you\u2019ll explore how a closed-loop
        (feedback) control system automatically adjusts pump power to maintain a
        desired flow rate. The system continuously compares the actual flow (from
        the flowmeter sensor) with the setpoint and corrects any error using a PID
        controller. This will help you understand the self-correcting nature of feedback
        systems.\""
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: 'This experiment aims to demonstrate the behavior of a closed-loop control
        system in a flow process and configure the system for automatic PID control,
        set a flow rate setpoint and observe how the controller maintains it. Introduce
        disturbances and observe how the system compensates. '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency stop button.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Turn on the main power switch of the unit.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_01
      value: Set initial PID gains to Kp=5, Ki=3, Kd=0.2.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetPoint_01
      value: Set the desired flow rate setpoint to 120 L/h.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: Click the 'Start' button to initiate the Pump.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button
      value: "Click on the \u201CSave Screen\u201D button to record system response
        characteristics."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Reset_Button_01
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_02
      value: Adjust Kp =0.5, Ki = 0.2,    Kd = 0.05.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: Click Start again.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Disturbance
      value: "Set the value to 30% using the \u201CDisturbance%\u201D slider."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Export_Button
      value: "Click \u201CExport\u201D to save the data to excel sheet."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished! You can now select another experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: Flow rate drops, then the PID controller increases pump power to restore
        the setpoint and minimize error.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: Observe the system's response on the graph. Note the rise time, overshoot,
        and steady-state error.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: What is the main advantage of a closed-loop control system over an open-loop
        system?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: Lower cost
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: Simpler design
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: Ability to self-correct using feedback
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: Which PID parameter most directly affects steady-state error?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: Kp
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: Ki
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: 'Kd '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button_02
      value: "Click \u201CSave Screen\u201D to capture the current response curve."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 536dfdbbddcc1ac4a859c8af22addfc8, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: "Flow Control in Open Loop\n\r(Manual Mode)\r\n"
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 2
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "Welcome! In this experiment, you\u2019ll explore how an open-loop control
        system operates without feedback. You\u2019ll manually control the pump power
        and observe how the flow rate responds directly to your input, with no automatic
        correction. This will help you understand the limitations of open-loop control
        in real-world applications."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: This experiment aims to demonstrate the behavior of an open-loop control
        system in a flow process, Observe the direct relationship between pump power
        and flow rate. And understand why open-loop systems cannot correct for disturbances.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency stop button.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Turn on the main power switch of the unit.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Manual_Mode_Button
      value: "Click the \u201COpen-Loop Mode\u201D button to disable PID and enter
        open-loop control."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Use_PumpAndFlow_Mode
      value: Activate switch in direction of flow rate
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetFlow_01
      value: Set the desired flow rate to 100 l/h.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Pump_01
      value: 'Adjust the pump slider to 60%. '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: Click the 'Start' button to initiate the pump.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Stop_Button_01
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Use_PumpOnly_Mode
      value: Activate switch in direction of Pump %.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Pump_02
      value: Set the desired flow rate to 100 l/h.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: Click Start again.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Disturbance_01
      value: "Set disturbance to 20% using the \u201CDisturbance%\u201D slider."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button
      value: "Click \u201CSave Screen\u201D to capture the current response curve."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Export_button
      value: "Click \u201CExport\u201D to save the data to excel sheet."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished! You can now select another experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: Observe flow rate on the rotameter.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: Flow rate increases proportionally; no automatic regulation occurs.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: What happens if you increase the pump percentage in manual mode?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: Flow rate decreases
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: 'Flow rate increases '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: Nothing happened
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: Why is the disturbance valve used in manual mode?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: To maintain constant pressure
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: 'To simulate real-world system disturbances '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: To turn off the pump
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_03
      value: This mode depends on determining the flow rate along the ruler by applying
        a constant pump power and calculating the time required for the device to
        reach a desired flow rate. The pump power is then disconnected after this
        time, and the final flow rate reached by the device is observed.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_04
      value: Use this mode when you want to drive the device by direct pump power,
        not by a flow rate value on the ruler.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c9cbb2a3998113b42833a230ae67d717, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: "Pressure Control in Open Loop\n\r(Manual Mode)\r"
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 2
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "Welcome! In this mode, you\u2019ll learn how to manually control the
        pump and disturbance valve to observe real-time pressure changes without
        automatic PID regulation. This helps you understand system behavior under
        direct human input."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: To operate the pump and disturbance valve manually using software sliders,
        observe real-time pressure response, and understand how manual inputs affect
        system stability and pressure dynamics.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Switch on the ON/OFF switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Manual_Mode_Button
      value: "Click the \u201COpen-Loop Mode\u201D button to disable PID and enter
        open-loop control."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Use_PumpAndPressure_Mode
      value: Activate switch in direction of Pressure
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetPressure_01
      value: Set the desired pressure to 0.5 bar.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Pump_01
      value: 'Adjust the pump slider to 30%. '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: Click the 'Start' button to initiate the pump.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Stop_Button_01
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Use_PumpOnly_Mode
      value: Activate switch in direction of Pump %
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Pump_02
      value: Set the Pump slider to 60%.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: Click Start again.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Disturbance_01
      value: "Set disturbance to 90% using the \u201CDisturbance%\u201D slider."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button
      value: "Click \u201CSave Screen\u201D to capture the current response curve."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Export_button
      value: "Click \u201CExport\u201D to save the data to excel sheet."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished! You can now analyze your results or select another
        experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: Observe pressure rise on the gauge.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: Note that the system does not automatically correct its position.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: Why is the disturbance valve used in manual mode?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: To maintain constant pressure
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: 'To simulate real-world system disturbances '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: To turn off the pump
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: What happens if you increase the pump percentage in manual mode?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: Pressure decreases
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: 'Pressure increases '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: System shuts down
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_03
      value: This mode depends on determining the pressure point along the ruler
        by applying a constant pump power and calculating the time required for the
        device to reach a desired pressure. The pump is then disconnected after this
        time, and the final pressure reached by the device is observed.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_04
      value: Use this mode when you want to drive the device by direct pump power,
        not by a pressure value on the ruler.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e0f35cb5367b0cf43bb2979d18aa3258, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Emergency_Switch_Title
      value: Emergency Button
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Emergency_Switch_Def
      value: A safety push button with a large mushroom head and latching action
        that immediately cuts power to motion for safety purposes.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: ON_OFF_Button_Title
      value: ON/OFF Button
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: ON_OFF_Button_Def
      value: Control button that turns the training device's control circuit on or
        off
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Fan_Indication_LED_Title
      value: Fan LED
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Fan_Indication_LED_Def
      value: Indicates that the fan is ON and air circulation/cooling airflow is
        active
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Peltier_Element_Title
      value: Peltier Element
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Peltier_Element_Def
      value: "The Peltier element is a thermoelectric cooler used to heat or cool
        the experiment tube, depending on the applied \nvoltage.\r"
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: PT100_Sensor_Title
      value: PT100 Sensor
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: PT100_Sensor_Def
      value: "The PT100 temperature sensors measure the temperature inside the experiment
        tube by converting the \rresistance of the sensor into a corresponding temperature
        reading.\r"
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Temperature_Gauge_Title
      value: Temperature Gauge
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Temperature_Gauge_Def
      value: "The temperature gauge provides a visual indication of the temperature
        inside the experiment tube.\r"
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: External_Fan_Title
      value: External Fan
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: External_Fan_Def
      value: A fan that transfers heat between the system and the ambient to provide
        disturbance to the system.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Schematic_Diagram_Title
      value: Schematic Diagram
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Schematic_Diagram_Def
      value: A visual representation of the components, their connections, and the
        flow of power or signals within the system.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Heating_Indication_LED_Title
      value: Heating LED
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Heating_Indication_LED_Def
      value: Indicates that the system is operating in heating mode and the controller
        is commanding heating.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Cooling_Indication_LED_Title
      value: Cooling LED
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Cooling_Indication_LED_Def
      value: Indicates that the system is operating in cooling mode and the controller
        is commanding cooling.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ee757b2896ed3c040ba908d9126b8459, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: 'Temperature Control Using PID

        (Automatic Mode)

'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 1
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: "Welcome! In this experiment, you\u2019ll explore how a closed-loop
        PID controller automatically adjusts Peltier power to maintain a desired
        temperature, even when disturbances like fan-induced cooling are introduced.
        You\u2019ll observe stability, error correction, and dynamic response in
        real time."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: This experiment aims to study the performance of a closed-loop temperature
        control system using a PID controller.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency stop button.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Turn on the power switch of the unit.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_01
      value: 'Set initial PID gains: Kp= 6, Ki =12, Kd = 0.'
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetPoint_01
      value: "Set the desired temperature setpoint to 30\xB0C using the setpoint
        input field."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: "Click the \u201CStart\u201D button to initiate Peltier module."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button_01
      value: "Click on the \u201CSave Screen\u201D button to record system response
        characteristics."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Reset_Button_01
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Gains_02
      value: Adjust Ki = 1.5, Kd = 2.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: Click Start again.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Disturbance
      value: "Disturb the system by increasing the fan speed to 30% using \u201CDisturbance\u201D
        slider."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetPoint_02
      value: "Now adjust the setpoint to 20 \xB0C"
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button_02
      value: "Click \u201CSave Screen\u201D to capture the current response curve."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Export_Button
      value: "Click \u201CExport\u201D to save the data to excel sheet."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished! You can now analyze your results or select another
        experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: In closed-loop control, the system continuously compares the actual
        temperature with the setpoint and automatically adjusts the Peltier power
        to minimize error.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: You can observe that the system is trying to return smoothly to the
        setpoint once again
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_03
      value: Note that the Cooling LED is lights up instead of heating which indicates
        that Peltier module voltage is reversed.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: What is the main advantage of a closed-loop control system over an open-loop
        system?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: Lower cost
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: Simpler design
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: 'Ability to self-correct using feedback '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: Which PID term is most effective at eliminating steady-state error?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: Proportional (Kp)
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: 'Integral (Ki) '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: Derivative (Kd)
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
  - table: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 79d83ad8001512f45ab2a0b51a37cd86, type: 2}
    tableContent:
    - key: Title
      value: "Temperature Control in Open Loop \r\n(Manual Mode)\r\n"
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Title_Header
      value: Experiment 2
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Instructor
      value: Welcome! In this experiment, you'll learn how open-loop temperature
        control works without feedback correction. You'll manually adjust the Peltier
        power and observe how the system responds to your inputs and external disturbances.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Objectives
      value: 'This experiment aims to study the behavior of a temperature process
        operating in open-loop mode and understand the effect of actuator input on
        the temperature without feedback correction. '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pull_Emergency
      value: Release the emergency switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Switch_On
      value: Switch on the ON/OFF switch.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Manual_Mode_Button
      value: "Click the \u201COpen-Loop Mode\u201D button to disable PID and enter
        open-loop control."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Use_PowerAndTemp_Mode
      value: Activate switch in direction of Temperature
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SetTemp_01
      value: "Set the desired temperature to 30 \xB0C."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Power_01
      value: Adjust the power % slider to 80%.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_01
      value: Click the 'Start' button to initiate the module.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Stop_Button_01
      value: Reset the current run.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Use_PowerOnly_Mode
      value: Activate switch in direction of Power %.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Start_Button_02
      value: Click Start again.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Set_Disturbance_01
      value: "Set disturbance to 90% using the \u201CDisturbance%\u201D slider."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: SaveScreen_button
      value: "Click \u201CSave Screen\u201D to capture the current response curve."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Export_button
      value: "Click \u201CExport\u201D to save the data to excel sheet."
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: You_are_done
      value: You have finished! You can now analyze your results or select another
        experiment.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_01
      value: Observe that the temperature rise to reach the desired temperature in
        a certain estimated time.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_02
      value: Observe temperature rise on the gauge.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_03
      value: Note that the system does not automatically correct its position.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01
      value: What happens if you increase the power percentage of the Peltier module
        in manual mode?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_A
      value: 'Temperature increases '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_B
      value: 'Temperature decreases '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_01_C
      value: Fan speed increases
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02
      value: Why is the disturbance valve used in manual mode?
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_A
      value: To increase the heat transfer rate
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_B
      value: 'To simulate real-world system disturbances '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_C
      value: 'To increase the fan speed '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Pop_up_Quiz_02_D
      value: 'All the above '
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_04
      value: This mode depends on determining the temperature along the gauge by
        applying a constant Peltier power and calculating the time required for the
        device to reach a desired temperature. The module is then disconnected after
        this time, and the final Temperature reached by the device is observed.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
    - key: Notification_05
      value: Use this mode when you want to drive the device by direct Peltier power,
        not by choosing a temperature value from the slider.
      audioValue: {fileID: 0}
      spriteValue: {fileID: 0}
